---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Publications | James Young">
  <Fragment slot="sidebar">
    <div class="nav-section">
      <h2 class="nav-section-title">Navigation</h2>
      <ul class="nav-list">
        <li>
          <a href="/foretodata/" class="nav-link">
            <span class="num">&larr;</span>
            <span>Back to Home</span>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/foretodata/about" class="nav-link">
            <span>About</span>
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="nav-section">
      <h2 class="nav-section-title">On This Page</h2>
      <ul class="nav-list">
        <li>
          <a href="#ml-bioinformatics" class="nav-link">
            <span>ML / Bioinformatics</span>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="#wet-lab" class="nav-link">
            <span>Wet Lab / Experimental</span>
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Fragment>

  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <header class="mb-12">
      <span class="text-terminal-accent font-mono text-sm">~/publications</span>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-bold text-terminal-text mt-4 mb-6">
        Publications
      </h1>
      <p class="text-terminal-dim text-sm">
        135+ citations &middot;
        <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=EyrW6pEAAAAJ&hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-terminal-accent hover:underline">Google Scholar</a>
      </p>
    </header>

    <article class="prose prose-invert prose-terminal">

      <h2 id="ml-bioinformatics" class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-terminal-text mt-8 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-terminal-accent">&#9655;</span> ML / Bioinformatics
      </h2>

      <div class="space-y-6 text-terminal-dim">
        <div>
          <p class="text-terminal-text font-medium mb-1">Crowdsourcing assessment of maternal blood multi-omics for predicting gestational age and preterm birth</p>
          <p class="text-sm">Tarca AL, et al. (including <strong class="text-terminal-text">Young J</strong>)</p>
          <p class="text-sm"><em>Cell Reports Medicine</em>, 2(6):100323, 2021</p>
          <p class="text-sm mt-2">Organized a team at SDSU for a biological ML competition. Feature engineering and modeling (XGBoost, neural networks) on high-dimensional multi-omics data to predict preterm birth risk and gestational age.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="text-terminal-text font-medium mb-1">Chromosome-level genome assembly of the Chinese three-keeled pond turtle (<em>Mauremys reevesii</em>)</p>
          <p class="text-sm">Liu J, et al. (including <strong class="text-terminal-text">Young J</strong>)</p>
          <p class="text-sm"><em>Molecular Ecology Resources</em>, 22(4):1596-1605, 2022</p>
          <p class="text-sm mt-2">Contributed genome assembly and synteny analysis on the SDSU HPC cluster.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="text-terminal-text font-medium mb-1">Secondary Metabolites Are Highly Predictive of Diazotrophic Cyanobacteria Strains</p>
          <p class="text-sm"><strong class="text-terminal-text">Young J</strong>, Gu L, Zhou R</p>
          <p class="text-sm"><em>In Submission</em>, 2023</p>
          <p class="text-sm mt-2">Extracted secondary metabolites from CyanoDB, mapped them to diazotrophic capability, and validated with leave-one-out cross-validation (~0.98 AUC on holdout).</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="text-terminal-text font-medium mb-1">Predicting Cyanobacterial FOX Genes with a Data-Centric Machine Learning Approach</p>
          <p class="text-sm"><strong class="text-terminal-text">Young J</strong>, Gu L, Zhou R</p>
          <p class="text-sm"><em>In Submission</em>, 2023</p>
          <p class="text-sm mt-2">Integrated proteomic, transcriptomic, and genomic promoter data to build a predictive model for FOX genes (~0.85 holdout AUC), validated on experimentally determined genes.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 id="wet-lab" class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-terminal-text mt-10 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-terminal-accent">&#9655;</span> Wet Lab / Experimental
      </h2>

      <div class="space-y-6 text-terminal-dim">
        <div>
          <p class="text-terminal-text font-medium mb-1">Harnessing Solar-Powered Oxic N<sub>2</sub>-fixing Cyanobacteria for the BioNitrogen Economy</p>
          <p class="text-sm"><strong class="text-terminal-text">Young J</strong>, Gu L, Gibbons W, Zhou R</p>
          <p class="text-sm"><em>Cyanobacteria Biotechnology</em>, 2021</p>
          <p class="text-sm mt-2">Synthesized the research landscape and economic case for industrial-scale biological nitrogen fixation.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="text-terminal-text font-medium mb-1">Unicellular Cyanobacteria Exhibit Light-Driven, Oxygen-Tolerant, Constitutive Nitrogenase Activity Under Continuous Illumination</p>
          <p class="text-sm"><strong class="text-terminal-text">Young J</strong>, Gu L, Hildreth M, Zhou R</p>
          <p class="text-sm"><em>bioRxiv</em> 619353</p>
          <p class="text-sm mt-2">Demonstrated a nitrogen-fixation phenotype tolerating net-oxygen gains. Used GCMS, oxygraph, controlled growth chambers, inhibition assays, proteomics, and network analysis.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="text-terminal-text font-medium mb-1">Identification of Cell Surface Sugars in N<sub>2</sub>-fixing Cyanobacterium <em>Cyanothece</em> ATCC 51142 Using Fluorescein Labeled Lectins</p>
          <p class="text-sm"><strong class="text-terminal-text">Young J</strong>, Gu L, Hildreth M, Zhou R</p>
          <p class="text-sm"><em>SDAOS</em> Conference Paper, 2018</p>
          <p class="text-sm mt-2">Used microscopy to quantify cell surface fluorescence under different lectin treatments to identify cell envelope polysaccharides relevant to nitrogen fixation.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
